{"id":456,"name":"finneon","speciesId":456,"dex":456,"form":"normal","generation":4,"types":["water"],"stats":{"hp":49,"attack":49,"defense":56,"special-attack":49,"special-defense":61,"speed":66},"abilities":[{"name":"swift-swim","hidden":false},{"name":"storm-drain","hidden":false},{"name":"water-veil","hidden":true}],"height":4,"weight":70,"baseExp":66,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/456.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/456.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/456.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/456.ogg","genus":"Wing Fish Pokémon","genusPt":"Pokémon Peixe Asa","flavor":[{"version":"diamond","text":"After long exposure to sunlight, the patterns on its tail fins shine vividly when darkness arrives."},{"version":"pearl","text":"The way its two tail fins flutter while it swims has earned it the nickname “BEAUTIFLY of the Sea.”"},{"version":"platinum","text":"The line running down its side can store sunlight. It shines vividly at night."},{"version":"heartgold","text":"Swimming and fluttering its two tail fins, it looks like a BEAUTIFLY. At night, the patterns on its tail fins softly shine."},{"version":"sun","text":"It absorbs sunlight with the pink areas of its skin, which then shine. This appears to be a form of camouflage."},{"version":"moon","text":"Its double tail fins propel its energetic jumps. When it breaks the surface of the sea, Wingull swoop down to grab it on the fly."},{"version":"ultra-sun","text":"When night falls, their pink patterns begin to shine. They’re popular with divers, so there are resorts that feed them to keep them close."},{"version":"ultra-moon","text":"It lures in prey with its shining tail fins. It stays near the surface during the day and moves to the depths when nig